Z||000018||LZeitgeist||11-14-2001||08:40 AM||||Nearly all the responses to his introduction thread are polite welcomes and even more polite requests to consider changing it.<P>Hopefully he will do so; otherwise I would hope that Cliff will agree and step in... I'm normally not one for four-letter word censorship - heck, I use'em more than I should, even here. But I feel a screenname with a vulgarity in it is inappropriate for nearly any public forum.<P>Just my two cents... time will tell.<P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000019||bocefas||11-14-2001||08:41 AM||||If that's the name he wants, that's his choice.  Don't be so oblivious to the fact that people actually **swear** now and again.  If you're worried about your children seeing it, I have bad news for you...chances are if they go to public school they've already seen/heard/said worse.||||reg||1
Z||000020||LZeitgeist||11-14-2001||08:48 AM||||My ears aren't 'virgin' in any sense of the word. However, *some* things are still inappropriate, no matter how far the world has gone to Hell in a handbasket.<P>Lines may be blurred these days, but they're still lines - and they've always been there for a reason. <P>Geeze, I can't believe we actually have to discuss this sort of junk and debate over it. Proof yet again that "Common sense ain't."||||reg||1
